1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,680
A report returned zero rows.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:06,000
Without receipts, Decider picked inspect
pipeline on three calls.

3
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,700
Each spent its one read and ended
unresolved.

4
00:00:09,713 --> 00:00:13,373
Decider serves from a private, always-on
Amazon SageMaker endpoint.

5
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,780
Amazon Bedrock Nova Lite narrates only
after completion.

6
00:00:17,387 --> 00:00:22,007
Offline, we ran every diagnostic and
trained LoRA plus Decider's choice head

7
00:00:22,007 --> 00:00:26,047
on verifier labels. At runtime, the
receipt removes one repeat;

8
00:00:26,487 --> 00:00:27,907
LoRA ranks what remains;

9
00:00:28,367 --> 00:00:29,527
the verifier owns truth.

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:34,140
The reusable recipe sends current state
and matching history to Decider.

11
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:37,320
Only a proven exact repeat is withheld
before selection.

12
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,540
A receipt cannot pick a tool.

13
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,060
Decider chooses from the remaining tools.

14
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:48,200
Run 1 happens once: one inference, 21.6
seconds of client time, one read,

15
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:49,050
Unresolved.

16
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:54,380
The deterministic verifier stored a
Decision Receipt: real data, no decision

17
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:56,480
moved. The model is unchanged.

18
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:58,860
The system recorded a fact.

19
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:02,300
Run 2 is a new call, and the exact receipt
matches.

20
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:06,540
Before the first Decider request and
before any read, the controller

21
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:08,620
precludes only the proven dead end.

22
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,780
Decider makes one fresh choice, inspect
schema keys.

23
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:17,860
One inference, one read, a verified
repair, completed in 26.6 seconds.

24
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:21,840
Old Run 2 took 54.8 seconds and two
inferences.

25
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:26,260
Optimized Run 2 takes 26.6 seconds and one
inference.

26
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:31,500
That is one fewer inference and an
observed difference of 28.2 seconds, or

27
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:34,060
51.4 percent lower client latency.

28
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,060
One synthetic case, each proof once.

29
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:42,107
Across 160 decisions, correct first
choices rose from 97 to

30
00:01:42,107 --> 00:01:47,587
129. Across 64 calls, wasted first reads
fell from 20 to 15

31
00:01:47,587 --> 00:01:50,187
and completions rose from 44 to 49;

32
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:54,867
CPU replay confirmed direction, one seed,
experimental checkpoint.

33
00:01:55,747 --> 00:01:57,627
One failed decision becomes a boundary.

34
00:01:58,207 --> 00:02:01,727
History can rule out one proven execution
under one identical context.

35
00:02:02,347 --> 00:02:03,667
It cannot choose the next tool.

36
00:02:03,667 --> 00:02:07,907
Decider chooses. The verifier decides what
the read found.
